{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTLcW6c5sq2y4ZS6DsQo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`test_large_sequence` fails because the test and the code disagree about what a 5-digit sequence number should produce.\n\n- The test expects `invoice_number(2026, 12345)` to return `\"INV-2026-2345\"`, which keeps only the last four digits.\n- The code returns `\"INV-2026-12345\"`. The format spec `:04` sets a minimum width of 4 digits and never truncates, so 12345 comes out in full.\n\nI did not change anything. The fix depends on which behavior you want:\n\n- **If sequences can exceed 9999, the test is wrong.** Truncating to `2345` makes invoice 12345 collide with invoice 2345. Change the expected value to `\"INV-2026-12345\"`.\n- **If numbers must always be exactly four digits, the code is wrong.** Wrap or reject the sequence, for example `f\"{seq % 10000:04}\"`, or raise an error when `seq > 9999`. Then the test's expectation holds, but the wrap still collides with earlier numbers, so raising an error is the safer choice.\n\nMy recommendation is the first option: the code is doing what a four-digit minimum padding should do, and the test asserts a silent wrap that would produce duplicate invoice numbers. Tell me which behavior you want and I'll make the change.\n\nI ran the tests with `python3 -m unittest -v test_invoice` because pytest is not installed here. `test_format` passes and `test_large_sequence` fails."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":656,"cache_read_input_tokens":40077,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":656},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6b0bf08-825f-4dee-89aa-106ae5371b1a","uui